Explanation:

From $(U_s + Omega R_E cos phi_s) R_E cos phi_s = (U_d + Omega R_E cos phi_d) R_E cos phi_d$, setting $U_s=0, phi_s=0$ yields $U_d = Omega R_E / cos(30 degree) - Omega R_E cos(30 degree) = 463/0.866 - 463(0.866) approx 125 "m/s"$.
